@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Nexa AI backend (`apps/ai`)
+
+## Configuration
+
+Settings come from environment variables. On startup the server loads `.env` files from the
+current directory up to the repository root, so the repo-root `.env` is found even though
+`npm run start:ai` runs from `apps/ai`. Variables already set in the shell win over files, and a
+nearer `.env` wins over one further up. See `.env.example` for every variable.
+
+## Provider errors
+
+Provider failures are normalised to `AIProviderError` (`apps/ai/core/errors.ts`) and returned to
+the client as JSON `{ "error": "<safe message>", "code": "<code>" }`. Upstream response text is
+logged on the server only.
+
+| code | HTTP | meaning | retried |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `config` | 503 | missing API key, unknown provider or model | no |
+| `auth` | 502 | provider rejected the credentials (401/403) | no |
+| `model_not_found` | 502 | provider says the model does not exist or is unavailable (404) | no |
+| `rate_limit` | 429 | provider rate limit (429) | yes |
+| `unavailable` | 503 | provider 5xx or network failure | yes |
+| `timeout` | 504 | no response within `DALTRON_AI_TIMEOUT_MS` | no |
+| `bad_request` | 502 | provider rejected the request (400) | no |
+| `unknown` | 502 | anything else | no |
+
+Retries use exponential backoff (`DALTRON_AI_RETRY_BASE_DELAY_MS`, doubling) up to
+`DALTRON_AI_MAX_RETRIES`. A timeout stops waiting but cannot cancel the upstream request, so
+timeouts are not retried.
+
+## Tests
+
+`npm test` builds `apps/ai` and runs `dist/tests/*.test.js` with the Node test runner. Tests use
+fake providers; none call Gemini or need an API key.
-- 
